     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation.\n\n**Why:** 5100 mg/day is twice the highest labeled dose of metformin. No accepted use calls for that much, and doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis. Errors like this, where a daily total gets entered as the amount for each dose, are a common cause of serious harm, so an exceeded maximum has to be caught before the order is placed, not after.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- **Enter a dose within the limit:** 850 mg three times daily with meals (2550 mg/day, the maximum), 1000 mg twice daily, or 850 mg twice daily (1700 mg/day total).\n- **If you have a specific reason for this dose,** please talk it over with the pharmacist on duty or your attending. If they approve it, it can go through the usual override process, with the reason documented by the prescriber who's responsible for it.\n\nWhich would you like? I can enter any of the doses above right away."
      }
     ],
